{
  "answer_text": "The evidence indicates that retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) does not consistently improve the factual accuracy of LLM-generated answers; its effectiveness varies significantly depending on the domain and the specific evaluation metric used. In some contexts, RAG reduces hallucinations, while in others, it decreases accuracy or fails to provide measurable benefits. Specifically, RAG reduced hallucination rates in science and history domains, but decreased accuracy in news, legal, and biomedical domains, and showed mixed or negligible results in trivia.",
